        "shape": "directory",
        "source": "https://cursor.com/docs/plugins",
        "note": "A local plugin is installed at `~/.cursor/plugins/local/<name>/` with either a root `plugin.json` or `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` inside it -- the `local/` level is the one the product reads, and the setups here write it. A plugin's manifest names its `rules`, `skills`, `agents`, `commands` and `hooks`; that manifest is how every one of those reaches the CLI, which is why none of them is a namespace of its own"
      },
      {
        "path": "plugins/local",
        "kinds": [],
        "shape": "directory",
        "source": "https://cursor.com/docs/plugins",
        "note": "The directory the product actually reads a local plugin from, and where the setups here write. Declared *beside* `plugins` rather than instead of it: the consumer validates a compiler's route by exact membership in native_namespaces, so declaring only one of the two refuses every install against a CLI carrying the other"
      }
    ],
    "declined": [
      {
        "path": "AGENTS.md",
        "reason": "The CLI reads AGENTS.md at the project root and upward, not from ~/.cursor. Global user rules are set in the application under Customize -> Rules and have no file under the config home; the absence is a standing community request.",
